description |
  bench/unusual@0.1 -- the unusual-features set. This file carries ONLY the
  `ext bench` capability matrix (the pattern source is subbench.toml's
  [[patterns]] array + patterns/*.rx); every block below is a verbatim copy of
  bench/capability/patterns.rxt's, so an engine fact is declared in one place
  (gen_patterns.py --check). The `callouts` token is declared for libpcre2 only:
  pcrec's callout binding and Oniguruma's `(?{N})` spelling are L5's to declare;
  the vars / unusual-<member> tokens are declared by L5/L7 (patterns carry them as requires-*).

oracle pcre2
tag set=unusual, version=0.1
ext bench
  roster pcre2-interp pcre2-jit pcrec-auto pcrec-nocaps pcrec-vm pcrec-vm-in re2-default onig-default vectorscan-block-som rust-default pcre2-interp-deep pcre2-jit-deep pcrec-auto-deep pcrec-vm-deep onig-default-deep
  capabilities pcre2-interp
    backrefs
    lookaround
    lookbehind-variable
    possessive-quantifier
    atomic-group
    recursion
    conditionals
    k-reset
    control-verbs
    unicode-properties
    named-groups
    free-spacing
    callouts
    span-reporting
    non-utf8-subject
    captures
    true-end-anchor
  capabilities pcre2-jit
    backrefs
    lookaround
    lookbehind-variable
    possessive-quantifier
    atomic-group
    recursion
    conditionals
    k-reset
    control-verbs
